      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "dct:type": {
        "@id": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5227332"
      },
      "rdfs:label": "Probis clustering",
      "sc:description": "Consider all possible protein pocket pairs in the Crossdocked2020 test set, excluding self-pairs, and compute their similarity using the ProBis algorithm as suggested in the original CrossDocked2020 paper. Based on the resulting Z-score similarity, we bin each pair into easy (Z-score < 2), medium (2 < Z-score < 3) and hard (3 < Z-score) categories, with higher similarity corresponding to harder test cases."
    }
